                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers. Spoiler Free Review. [/h1]\n\n[b]Cheap scare, how much is it worth to you?[/b] So in this game, you have a flashlight and a hidden key to look for to open the gates and escape the camp. [u]The key is in randomized locations throughout Camp Waddalooh.[/u] I'm not sure of all the random locations it can be located within the camp, but it seems to be at least in one of 3 main areas. \n\nThe whole map is pretty small. You walk at a decent rate and you can also run albeit not that much faster than the walking speed. There's this monster than you can hear around you. You do the obvious thing when you see it ... you know .... do I really need to tell you? Spoiler alert [spoiler] Duh, you shine your flashlight at it and it runs away ... monster is scared of the light [/spoiler]\n\nIf you don't do what you're supposed to do, then bam, you know what happens next (spoiler alert: [spoiler] you get a jump scare ... obvi! [/spoiler] You can hear the monster and the audio seemed to be spatial to me at least I could always tell where it was coming from. But you know that thing that happens in horror games .. you know that mechanic .... you know .. do I really need to tell you? Spoiler alert [spoiler] yeah your flashlight starts acting up, batteries are momentarily dying so don't run out of light when the monster is near [/spoiler]\n\nSo there is some replayability here. Honestly, this is the kind of game that is fun to have an unsuspecting friend / relative come over and play. Then you can laugh at them when they nearly have a heart attack. Is that worth $4.99? Meh, there's better versions of this game like Raptor Valley (it has a lower sale price currently) ... so buy on sale. \n\nRate 5/10. This should be a $1.99 game and then .99 cents sale and then I'd give a higher rating. Still not bad. Not good either, but not too shabby on sale. If you're a cheesy horror fan, then definitely get it.\n\n",
